{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>וְנוֹדְעָה הַחַטָּאת אֲשֶׁר חָטְאוּ עָלֶיהָ</b> — it is obvious that they do not bring a sin-offering until they know that they have sinned. But the way of the language is that Scripture says: when it becomes known to them that they have sinned, they shall bring their offering. And it did not state thus regarding the anointed priest, because there is no need. And it is possible that Scripture commands that they are not liable for this sin-offering except upon knowledge, not upon uncertainty like a suspensive guilt-offering. And our Sages expounded (Sifra here): if they knew that they [the court] had ruled but did not know what they ruled — one might think they are liable; therefore Scripture says, 'וְנוֹדְעָה הַחַטָּאת' — and not merely that the sinners became aware. And it did not state thus regarding the anointed priest, because it says (Leviticus 4:3), 'לְאַשְׁמַת הָעָם' — behold, the anointed priest is like the congregation."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:50:11.428663425Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}